problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite set $$\mathcal{V}$$ of vehicle types, indexed by $$i \in \mathcal{V}$$.
- A group of $$N$$ travelers must be transported in a single planning decision.
- Each vehicle type $$i$$ has a seating capacity $$c_i$$, a rental cost $$k_i$$, and an available fleet limit $$u_i$$.
- A total of $$D$$ drivers are available.
- Each rented vehicle requires one driver.
- The goal is to choose how many vehicles of each type to rent so that all travelers are accommodated at minimum total rental cost.
- The chosen fleet must respect the available number of vehicles of each type.
- The total number of rented vehicles must not exceed the number of available drivers.
- The total seating capacity of the chosen vehicles must be sufficient for all travelers.
- All decision quantities must be nonnegative integers.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_i$$: the number of vehicles rented of type $$i \in \mathcal{V}$$.
  - $$z$$: the total rental cost of the selected fleet.

Input Format
{
  "demand": {
    "travelers": "$$N$$"
  },
  "resources": {
    "drivers_available": "$$D$$"
  },
  "vehicle_types": [
    {
      "type_id": "$$i$$",
      "available_units": "$$u_i$$",
      "capacity": "$$c_i$$",
      "rental_cost": "$$k_i$$"
    }
  ]
}

The array $$vehicle\_types$$ contains one record for each vehicle type $$i \in \mathcal{V}$$.

Output Format
{
  "selected_units": [
    {
      "type_id": "$$i$$",
      "quantity": "$$x_i$$"
    }
  ],
  "total_rental_cost": "$$z$$"
}

The array $$selected\_units$$ contains one record for each vehicle type $$i \in \mathcal{V}$$, giving the chosen integer quantity of that type.

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "demand": {
    "travelers": 400
  },
  "resources": {
    "drivers_available": 9
  },
  "vehicle_types": [
    {
      "type_id": "bus",
      "available_units": 10,
      "capacity": 50,
      "rental_cost": 800
    },
    {
      "type_id": "minibus",
      "available_units": 8,
      "capacity": 40,
      "rental_cost": 600
    }
  ]
}
